TreeSet internally uses a Red-Black Tree, a type of self-balancing binary search tree.

--For TreeSet or Treemap must implement Comparable

But your Student class does not implement Comparable,
so when TreeMap or TreeSet tries to sort it, it fails.

2️⃣ What happens internally

Inside TreeMap.put() or TreeSet.add(), the code calls something like:

compare(key1, key2);


If no Comparator was provided, it tries to cast the key (or element) to Comparable:

((Comparable) key1).compareTo(key2);


But since your Student class doesn’t implement Comparable,
that cast fails → ClassCastException.


TreeSet<Student> set = new TreeSet<>(Comparator.comparing(s -> s.id));
